Hi
I'm still looking, but here are a couple of notes. The size of your
mask is due to the polygon data - this is unnecessary and can be
suppressed with keep.poly = FALSE in make.mask, or retrospectively
with
attr(TiogaMask.comb.km <http://TiogaMask.comb.km>[[1]], 'polygon') <- NULL
attr(TiogaMask.comb.km <http://TiogaMask.comb.km>[[2]], 'polygon') <- NULL

I found working with your km datasets confusing (and a possible source
of trouble) so I reverted to metres.

There seem to be no recaptures between clusters of detectors (these
could if necessary be modelled as separate 'sessions'). That also
raises the possibility that clusters were too small to span the scale
of movements. That might be an argument for including the telemetry
data, but the clash between different estimates of sigma is suspicious
and relying telemetry for salvation seems ad hoc to me.

Murray

